betterquesting:10.desc:8:
Raw Hyperdense Stellar Plasma is too loose to seed a neutron star, so finish it inside a black hole. The Kerr Compressor Module runs §9Kerr Densification§r, only on a §9Kerr T2 holding at least 128 SM§r:
-§9 10,000 L Raw Hyperdense Stellar Plasma + 288 L molten SpaceTime + 64 Neutronium bolts → 1,000 L Hyperdense Stellar Mixture§r, 20 s at UMV, before the hole's bonus.

Hyperdense Stellar Mixture (HSM) is used for:
- the Core Collapse's neutron seed (5,000 L);
- feeding the neutron star (0-1.5 L/s);
- the Galactic Upgrade Core (32,000 L, as its condensate);
- Galactic Shell Plating and Star Chart: Neutron Star.

[note]Raise the KEE's setpoint to 128 SM or more before you start: below that the module refuses the recipe.[/note]

§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r you hold 1,000 L of Hyperdense Stellar Mixture.

Eye T7's harvest. Its uses:
- the Conduit's throat fuel after T7 (0.25 / 1 / 4 L/s per element);
- Eye T8's feed (0-10 L/s);
- the Mk III throat;
- with Beyond the Stars' Eye, the input of the §9Eternity§r loop: the Temporal Harmonizer Catalyst takes 9,216 L of Ergomatter and the Plasma Forge's Timepiece 4,608 L, instead of Universium.

A quasar-linked Kerr T2 refines it into Superdense Ergomatter at 8 : 1 (see §cSuperdense Ergomatter, the Slow Way§r).

§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r you have 16,000 L of Ergomatter.

The pack's§9 4096A UXV laser hatches§r carry more power than any energy hatch. The pack's own recipe needs UXV parts (Universium, Eye T10), so this one does not (Assembly Line, UXV):
- Target: 2 UMV Energy Hatches, 32 UMV Sensors, 8 UXV circuits, 16 UXV Superconductor Wire;
- Source: 2 UMV Dynamo Hatches, 32 UMV Emitters, the same circuits and wire;
- each with 2,304 L Magnetar Matter and 32,000 L Antipolarization Agent (about 2 h of one T6).

[note]On a Kerr module the tier of the total input (voltage × amps) sets the parallels: a 4096A UXV laser counts as tier 19.[/note]

§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r you hold a 4096A UXV Laser Target Hatch and its Source Hatch.

The control box takes 2 §9Directive Hatches§r and 2 §9Stellar Field Sensor Hatches§r. The console's E dial is the Eddington balance; the flux bar fills to an eruption at 100 (one tick marks your purge setpoint, another the 90 warning).

§5§lQUASAR: §lDISC§r The Directive Hatch's set (window w in its GUI, default 5). Each code adds its bits:
- [1] E < -w: pulse the feed gas;
- [2] E > +w: a Space trim;
- [4] the flux at your purge setpoint: purge;
- [8] alarm: a blow-out or re-forming, no coil power, a jet venting, a conduit element closed.

§5§lSENSOR§r E, the flux, λ, a, M, Bu/t, the eruption warning, seconds to the next eruption, the best host's σ and the link streak: analog with a window, or 15 above / below a threshold; invert flips it.

A comparator reads the Directive code; Steve's Factory Manager reads it as an analog range.

§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r you hold a Directive Hatch (HOLD → CLAIM → INSTALL).

With OpenComputers, an Adapter against a Beyond the Stars machine (the Eye, the Kerr, the quasar, a conduit element, a crown, a receptor port, the Homogeny, Reality Diffraction, a Directive or Sensor hatch) gives a component. Setters take one call a second (the field's step); a refused call returns nil and the reason.
- bts_quasar: getDisc, getBurst, getFeed, setFeed, setGas, setField, trim, purge, getLinks, getMilestones, getDirective; with a lattice also getBand, getIntake, getHoldUp, getBuffer, getOverdrive, getAnchor, getHorizon, setMassSetpoint, setOverdrive, setUnbound, shed;
- bts_eye: getState, getField, getBuffers, getEvent, getUnlock, getDirective, beginTransition, setDial, setFeed, setFeed8, setMode, trim, getSlots;
- bts_mouth and bts_mirror: getLink, getThroat, getUpkeep, setFuel, isOpen;
- bts_junction: getFlow, setRatio, setGain, setOut3, setLimit, setMode;
- bts_crown (getPower, getStream, getMk), bts_receptor (getDelivery), bts_homogeny, bts_reality, bts_kerr (getState().link), bts_directive and bts_sensor.

[note]Optional: the logic-gate rig needs no computer.[/note]

§2§lDONE §lWHEN§r you have read one of these from a computer (tick the box).

ops.desc:
§lFirst §lLight.§r Sol's product: 50,000 L a cycle × your yield. NEI calls it Condensed Raw Stellar Plasma Mixture, and the Eye's GUI and tooltips call it Raw Star Matter.

It goes into:
- Sirius A's upkeep (25,000 L a cycle);
- the §9Stellar Mass Core§r that unlocks T2 (256,000 L);
- the §9Kerr Density Upgrade§r (4,000,000 L);
- Beam Band and Jet Crescent casings, star charts, and Sirius B's overshoot trim;
- the Stellar Catalyst, as before.
For the Condensate Assembler it is condensed 1 : 1 into §9Entangled Raw Star Matter§r first (NEI: Condensate Entanglement).

[note]Your first milestone is counting already: §l20,000,000 §lL§r made on this Eye and §l2 §lh §lResonant§r open the road to T2.[/note]
